ll,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.00470231121365039,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":41.9,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04154045142677997,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":57.3,"_gate_share_shrink":0.004449411234561218,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":44.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.006494927392082753,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":89.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.067779996,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":45.2,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"BayCom Corp operates as the bank holding company for United Business Bank that provides various financial services to small and mid-sized businesses, service professionals, and individuals. The company provides demand, savings, money market, and time deposit accounts. It also offers commercial and multifamily real estate loans, including owner-occupied and investor real estate loans; commercial and industrial loans, such as equipment loans and working capital lines of credit; small business administration loans; construction and land loans; agriculture-related loans; and consumer loans comprising installment loans, unsecured and secured personal lines of credit, and overdraft protection. In addition, the company provides online and mobile banking, automated teller machine, remote deposit capture, night depository, courier, and direct deposit services; treasury management services that includes balance reporting, transfers between accounts, wire transfer initiation, automated clearing house (ACH) origination, and stop payments; debit cards; cashier's and travelers checks; letters of credit; and lockbox, positive pay, reverse positive pay, and account reconciliation services, as well as zero balance accounts and sweep accounts, including loan sweep. It operates through a network of full-service banking branches in Northern and Southern California; Las Vegas, Nevada; Denver, Colorado; Custer, Delta, and Grand counties, Colorado; and Seattle, Washington and Central New Mexico. The company was formerly known as Bay Commercial Bank and changed its name to BayCom Corp in January 2017. BayCom Corp was incorporated in 2004 and is headquartered in Walnut Creek, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christopher F. Baron | President, CEO & Director | Age 55","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 323 people. Revenue per employee of $311K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $93K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["BayCom Corp is a small-cap financial services business with a $325M market cap on $101M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are expanding by +2.3pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $30M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 30 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.33\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 6.8% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $1.8M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Bay Commercial Bank (NASDAQ:BCML) Director Michael Perdue Buys 5,000 Shares of Company Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/bay-commercial-bank-nasdaqbcml-director-michael-perdue-buys-5000-shares-of-company-stock.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795177614.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.91,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(BCML) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/35/BCML_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_112026010802_1795154882.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795154882.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Are Finance Stocks Lagging  Bay Commercial Bank (BCML) This Year?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3031032/are-finance-stocks-lagging-bay-commercial-bank-bcml-this-year?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_1-3031032","date":"2026-11-17","timestamp":1794922803.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"SR Bancorp (NASDAQ:SRBK) & Bay Commercial Bank (NASDAQ:BCML) Financial Analysis","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/15/sr-bancorp-nasdaqsrbk-bay-commercial-bank-nasdaqbcml-financial-analysis.html","date":"2026-11-16","timestamp":1794788091.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Technical Reactions to BCML Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/89/Technical_Reactions_to_BCML_Trends_in_Macro_Strategies_111026021001_1794294601.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794294601.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0